.TH ADVANCED-IP-ANALYSER 1 "September 2026" "Advanced IP Analyser 2.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
advanced-ip-analyser \- discover and inventory authorized network hosts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B advanced-ip-analyser
.I scan TARGET
[
.B --timeout SECONDS
]
[
.B --workers COUNT
]
[
.B --output FILE
]
.br
.B advanced-ip-analyser wake MAC
[
.B --broadcast ADDRESS
]
.br
.B advanced-ip-analyser capture TARGET
[
.B --interface NAME
]
[
.B --port PORT
]
[
.B --duration SECONDS
]
[
.B --max-packets COUNT
]
[
.B --output FILE
]
.br
.B advanced-ip-analyser capture-interfaces
.br
.B advanced-ip-analyser open-capture FILE
[
.B --host ADDRESS
]
[
.B --port PORT
]
[
.B --limit COUNT
]
[
.B --filter EXPRESSION
]
.br
.B advanced-ip-analyser watch
[
.B --interface NAME
]
[
.B --duration SECONDS
]
[
.B --snaplen BYTES
]
[
.B --report FILE
]
.br
.B advanced-ip-analyser analyse-capture FILE --report FILE
.br
.B advanced-ip-analyser web-audit URL --report FILE
[
.B --max-pages COUNT
]
[
.B --max-depth COUNT
]
[
.B --exclude PATH
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Advanced IP Analyser scans an IPv4 or IPv6 address, CIDR, or inclusive range,
identifies reachable devices and common TCP services, and exports inventories.
Use it only on networks and systems you own or are authorized to administer.
.SH GUI
Run
.B advanced-ip-analyser-gui
for the Debian desktop interface, saved devices, service launchers,
Wake-on-LAN, SSH power actions, and automatic updates.
The built-in Linux packet engine creates bounded live captures for selected
hosts and services and inspects Ethernet PCAP, PCAPNG, and compressed capture files.
Network Watch records bounded traffic over time, stores session history, and reports
flows, devices, DNS activity, TCP health, baselines, findings, and user alert rules.
The passive Wi-Fi window can observe access points and clients with a compatible
monitor-mode adapter; it never transmits deauthentication or injected frames.
The Web Security Audit performs an explicitly authorized, same-host, bounded,
read-only crawl and reports defensive HTTP, TLS, header, cookie, content, and
form observations. It does not submit forms or send exploit payloads.
.SH DISPLAY FILTERS
The packet viewer and
.B open-capture --filter
support IP addresses, TCP/UDP ports, DNS, HTTP, TLS handshakes, TCP flags, frame
lengths, comparisons, text matching, AND (&&), OR (||), NOT (!), and parentheses.
Display filters do not change the saved capture.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.config/advanced-ip-analyser/favorites.json
stores the current user's saved devices.
.br
.I ~/.config/advanced-ip-analyser/packet-filters.json
stores named packet display filters.
.br
.I ~/.local/share/advanced-ip-analyser/network-watch.sqlite3
stores Network Watch history.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ping (8),
.BR tracepath (8),
.BR ssh (1)
